# Part 11's control arm RUNS this program (panel 226's R1, 2026-10-20): the
# strict build refuses it under `never_rebound`, a thesis rule, and the control arm,
# `build --permissive`, gives the dropped rule the meaning the sitting's
# table pins: a cell nothing re-binds is a binding: its value is read as written.
# The witness is the compiler-engineer's (w19-never_rebound), one of 27 it ran before the
# resolution was written (`docs/panel/226-reports/compiler-engineer.md`).

function keep(@n: i64) -> i64  #~ never_rebound
    return n

function main()
    v: i64 @= 1
    print(keep(@v))
